## What This Is

Open-source self-hosted trading software for local data, manual order workflows, automation, AI-assisted analysis, and broker-gateway testing.
FlintTrade owns its backend and supports OpenAlgo as an optional external integration. 18 package surfaces (13 Python + 3 apps + 1 shared TypeScript design system + 1 Rust/PyO3 tick engine), monorepo, AGPL-3.0.
Repo: https://github.com/navaneeshnagarajan/FlintTrade

Serves three trading-software modes from a single application:
- **Trader** — Manual order workflows, intraday tools, options analysis, and Live-mode safeguards
- **Automator** — Strategy development, sandbox testing, broker-gateway testing, and AI-assisted workflows
- **Learner** — Guided market concepts, paper trading, and glossary support

One app. One port. Route-based separation. Widget-composable workspace.

## Architecture

FlintTrade runs its own backend first. OpenAlgo is optional and external.

- **OpenAlgo:** Optional broker connections, REST API port 5000, WebSocket port 8765
- **FlintTrade:** Single React app (FlexLayout workspace) + Python backend (strategy engine, backtesting, AI, data pipelines, screener, multi-account orchestration)
- **External test-deps (not bundled, not submodules):** OpenAlgo is an optional external service FlintTrade can talk to over HTTP/WS. Contributors can run `scripts/setup-test-deps.sh` to clone a local-dev copy into `.local/external/openalgo/` (gitignored, not shipped). AlgoMirror is intentionally absent — its mirroring patterns are absorbed into `packages/services/ditto/` and run in-process; the upstream repo is no longer tracked.
- OpenAlgo is needed only for the optional OpenAlgo-compatible integration path. Native backend, site, terminal, docs, design-system, and most unit tests run without it.

```
                                ┌─ native gateway (BrokerAdapter) ──> Broker API
FlintTrade (React + Python) ────┤
                                └─ OpenAlgo bridge adapter (optional) ──> OpenAlgo (port 5000) ──> Broker API
```

### Application Routes

```
localhost:5173/
├── /welcome        → First-time cinematic welcome (smart redirect)
├── /explore        → Demo mode with sample data (no broker needed)
├── /setup          → First-time wizard (Quick / Guided / Advanced)
├── /settings       → Standalone settings page
├── /trade          → Trader workspace (FlexLayout canvas; catalogue in widgetFactory.tsx)
├── /invest         → Investor dashboard (holdings, net worth, SIPs)
├── /learn          → Beginner center (courses, glossary, strategies)
├── /lab            → Strategy Lab (backtest, forward test, optimize)
├── /automate       → Automation Hub (flows, cron, monitors, logs)
├── /ai             → AI Center (chat, signals, sentiment, RAG)
├── /ditto          → Multi-account management (mirror, margin, risk)
├── /admin          → Admin panel (security, health, traffic, audit)
└── *               → 404 catch-all
```

All routes share: design system, API layer, auth state, WebSocket connection.
Each route lazy-loads its own module. No cross-route code in the initial bundle.

